# Authentication Patterns Guidelines

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này định nghĩa các nguyên tắc và best practices cho việc implement authentication systems trong Cursor Enterprise Framework. Mục tiêu là đảm bảo secure user identity management, protection against attacks, và compliance với security standards.

Authentication là quá trình xác minh identity của user hoặc system. Việc implement authentication đúng cách là nền tảng của application security và user trust.

## Nguyên tắc cơ bản

### 1. Multi-Layer Authentication

Implement defense in depth với multiple authentication factors.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Authentication Layers                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                             │
│  Layer 1: Knowledge Factor (Something you know)            │
│  └── Password, PIN, Security Questions                     │
│                                                             │
│  Layer 2: Possession Factor (Something you have)           │
│  └── TOTP, SMS Code, Hardware Token, Email Link            │
│                                                             │
│  Layer 3: Inherence Factor (Something you are)             │
│  └── Fingerprint, Face ID, Retina Scan                    │
│                                                             │
│  Layer 4: Behavioral Factor (Something you do)            │
│  └── Typing patterns, Mouse movements                     │
│                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2. Password Security

Strong password hashing và storage.

```typescript
// Password hashing with bcrypt
import bcrypt from 'bcrypt';

const SALT_ROUNDS = 12;

async function hashPassword(password: string): Promise<string> {
    return bcrypt.hash(password, SALT_ROUNDS);
}

async function verifyPassword(
    password: string,
    hashedPassword: string
): Promise<boolean> {
    return bcrypt.compare(password, hashedPassword);
}

// Modern password hashing with Argon2
import argon2 from 'argon2';

async function hashPasswordArgon2(password: string): Promise<string> {
    return argon2.hash(password, {
        type: argon2.argon2id,
        memoryCost: 65536,    // 64MB
        timeCost: 3,           // 3 iterations
        parallelism: 4        // 4 parallel threads
    });
}

async function verifyPasswordArgon2(
    password: string,
    hashedPassword: string
): Promise<boolean> {
    return argon2.verify(hashedPassword, password);
}
```

```typescript
// Password strength validation
import { z } from 'zod';

const passwordSchema = z.string()
    .min(8, 'Password must be at least 8 characters')
    .max(128, 'Password must be less than 128 characters')
    .regex(/[a-z]/, 'Password must contain at least one lowercase letter')
    .regex(/[A-Z]/, 'Password must contain at least one uppercase letter')
    .regex(/[0-9]/, 'Password must contain at least one number')
    .regex(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/, 'Password must contain at least one special character');

function validatePasswordStrength(password: string): ValidationResult {
    const result = passwordSchema.safeParse(password);

    if (!result.success) {
        return {
            valid: false,
            errors: result.error.issues.map(i => i.message)
        };
    }

    // Additional checks
    const commonPasswords = ['password', '12345678', 'qwerty123', 'admin123'];
    if (commonPasswords.includes(password.toLowerCase())) {
        return { valid: false, errors: ['Password is too common'] };
    }

    return { valid: true, errors: [] };
}
```

### 3. JWT Token Management

Secure JWT implementation.

```typescript
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';
import { nanoid } from 'nanoid';

interface TokenPayload {
    sub: string;         // User ID
    email: string;
    role: string;
    type: 'access' | 'refresh';
    jti: string;         // Unique token ID
}

interface TokenPair {
    accessToken: string;
    refreshToken: string;
    expiresIn: number;
}

const ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY = '15m';
const REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY = '7d';
const REFRESH_TOKEN_ROTATION_EXPIRY = '30d';

class TokenService {
    constructor(
        private config: AuthConfig,
        private redis: RedisClient
    ) {}

    async generateTokens(user: User): Promise<TokenPair> {
        const accessTokenId = nanoid();
        const refreshTokenId = nanoid();

        const accessToken = jwt.sign(
            {
                sub: user.id,
                email: user.email,
                role: user.role,
                type: 'access',
                jti: accessTokenId
            } as TokenPayload,
            this.config.jwtSecret,
            { expiresIn: ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY }
        );

        const refreshToken = jwt.sign(
            {
                sub: user.id,
                email: user.email,
                type: 'refresh',
                jti: refreshTokenId
            },
            this.config.jwtSecret,
            { expiresIn: REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY }
        );

        // Store refresh token in Redis for revocation
        await this.redis.setex(
            `refresh:${refreshTokenId}`,
            7 * 24 * 60 * 60, // 7 days
            JSON.stringify({
                userId: user.id,
                createdAt: Date.now()
            })
        );

        return {
            accessToken,
            refreshToken,
            expiresIn: 15 * 60 // seconds
        };
    }

    async verifyAccessToken(token: string): Promise<TokenPayload> {
        try {
            const payload = jwt.verify(token, this.config.jwtSecret) as TokenPayload;

            // Check token type
            if (payload.type !== 'access') {
                throw new AuthError('Invalid token type');
            }

            return payload;
        } catch (error) {
            if (error instanceof jwt.TokenExpiredError) {
                throw new TokenExpiredError();
            }
            if (error instanceof jwt.JsonWebTokenError) {
                throw new InvalidTokenError();
            }
            throw error;
        }
    }

    async refreshTokens(refreshToken: string): Promise<TokenPair> {
        // Verify refresh token
        const payload = jwt.verify(
            refreshToken,
            this.config.jwtSecret
        ) as TokenPayload & { jti: string };

        if (payload.type !== 'refresh') {
            throw new AuthError('Invalid token type');
        }

        // Check if token is blacklisted
        const isBlacklisted = await this.redis.get(`blacklist:${payload.jti}`);
        if (isBlacklisted) {
            throw new InvalidTokenError('Token has been revoked');
        }

        // Get user
        const user = await this.userService.findById(payload.sub);
        if (!user) {
            throw new AuthError('User not found');
        }

        // Invalidate old refresh token
        await this.redis.del(`refresh:${payload.jti}`);

        // Generate new tokens
        return this.generateTokens(user);
    }

    async revokeToken(tokenId: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.redis.setex(`blacklist:${tokenId}`, 86400, '1');
    }

    async revokeAllUserTokens(userId: string): Promise<void> {
        const keys = await this.redis.keys(`refresh:*:${userId}*`);
        if (keys.length > 0) {
            await this.redis.del(...keys);
        }
    }
}
```

### 4. OAuth 2.0 Implementation

OAuth 2.0 flow implementation.

```typescript
// OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code Flow
import { oauth2Client } from './oauth-client';
import { createHash, randomBytes } from 'crypto';

class OAuthService {
    constructor(
        private config: OAuthConfig,
        private stateStore: StateStore,
        private tokenService: TokenService
    ) {}

    // Step 1: Generate authorization URL
    async getAuthorizationUrl(
        provider: OAuthProvider,
        redirectUri: string,
        state?: string
    ): Promise<{ url: string; state: string }> {
        const stateNonce = state || randomBytes(32).toString('hex');
        const codeVerifier = randomBytes(32).toString('base64url');
        const codeChallenge = createHash('sha256')
            .update(codeVerifier)
            .digest('base64url');

        // Store state and verifier
        await this.stateStore.set(`oauth:${provider}:${stateNonce}`, {
            codeVerifier,
            redirectUri,
            createdAt: Date.now()
        });

        const url = oauth2Client[provider].createAuthorizationURL({
            redirectUri,
            scope: this.getScopes(provider),
            state: stateNonce,
            codeChallenge
        });

        return { url, state: stateNonce };
    }

    // Step 2: Handle callback
    async handleCallback(
        provider: OAuthProvider,
        code: string,
        state: string
    ): Promise<TokenPair> {
        // Verify state
        const storedState = await this.stateStore.get(`oauth:${provider}:${state}`);
        if (!storedState) {
            throw new AuthError('Invalid state parameter');
        }

        const { codeVerifier, redirectUri } = storedState;

        // Exchange code for tokens
        const tokens = await oauth2Client[provider].exchangeCode(
            code,
            codeVerifier,
            redirectUri
        );

        // Get user info
        const userInfo = await oauth2Client[provider].getUserInfo(tokens.accessToken);

        // Find or create user
        const user = await this.userService.findOrCreateOAuthUser(
            provider,
            userInfo
        );

        // Clean up state
        await this.stateStore.del(`oauth:${provider}:${state}`);

        // Generate application tokens
        return this.tokenService.generateTokens(user);
    }

    private getScopes(provider: OAuthProvider): string[] {
        const scopes: Record<OAuthProvider, string[]> = {
            google: ['openid', 'email', 'profile'],
            github: ['read:user', 'user:email'],
            microsoft: ['openid', 'email', 'profile'],
            facebook: ['email', 'public_profile']
        };
        return scopes[provider];
    }
}
```

### 5. Session Management

Secure session handling.

```typescript
import session from 'express-session';
import RedisStore from 'connect-redis';

class SessionService {
    constructor(private redis: RedisClient) {}

    getSessionConfig(): session.SessionOptions {
        return {
            store: new RedisStore({
                client: this.redis,
                prefix: 'session:'
            }),
            secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET!,
            name: 'cursor.sid',
            resave: false,
            saveUninitialized: false,
            cookie: {
                secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',
                httpOnly: true,
                sameSite: 'strict',
                maxAge: 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000, // 24 hours
                path: '/'
            },
            genid: () => nanoid(32)
        };
    }

    async invalidateSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.redis.del(`session:${sessionId}`);
    }

    async refreshSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {
        const sessionData = await this.redis.get(`session:${sessionId}`);
        if (sessionData) {
            await this.redis.expire(`session:${sessionId}`, 24 * 60 * 60);
        }
    }
}
```

### 6. Multi-Factor Authentication

MFA implementation với TOTP và backup codes.

```typescript
import speakeasy from 'speakeasy';
import QRCode from 'qrcode';
import { authenticator } from 'otplib';

class MFAService {
    constructor(
        private userService: UserService,
        private redis: RedisClient
    ) {}

    // Generate TOTP secret
    async generateMFASecret(userId: string): Promise<{
        secret: string;
        qrCode: string;
        backupCodes: string[];
    }> {
        const secret = authenticator.generateSecret();

        // Generate backup codes
        const backupCodes = Array.from({ length: 10 }, () =>
            randomBytes(8).toString('hex').toUpperCase()
        );

        // Hash backup codes for storage
        const hashedBackupCodes = await Promise.all(
            backupCodes.map(code => bcrypt.hash(code, 10))
        );

        // Generate QR code
        const user = await this.userService.findById(userId);
        const qrCode = await QRCode.toDataURL(
            authenticator.keyuri(user.email, 'Cursor', secret)
        );

        // Store secret (encrypted)
        await this.redis.setex(
            `mfa:pending:${userId}`,
            600, // 10 minutes to confirm
            JSON.stringify({
                secret,
                backupCodes: hashedBackupCodes
            })
        );

        return { secret, qrCode, backupCodes };
    }

    // Enable MFA
    async enableMFA(userId: string, token: string): Promise<boolean> {
        const pending = await this.redis.get(`mfa:pending:${userId}`);
        if (!pending) {
            throw new AuthError('No pending MFA setup');
        }

        const { secret } = JSON.parse(pending);

        // Verify token
        const isValid = authenticator.verify({ token, secret });
        if (!isValid) {
            throw new InvalidTokenError('Invalid MFA token');
        }

        // Update user
        await this.userService.update(userId, {
            mfaEnabled: true,
            mfaSecret: await this.encryptSecret(secret)
        });

        // Remove pending setup
        await this.redis.del(`mfa:pending:${userId}`);

        // Log security event
        await this.logSecurityEvent(userId, 'MFA_ENABLED');

        return true;
    }

    // Verify MFA token
    async verifyMFA(userId: string, token: string): Promise<boolean> {
        const user = await this.userService.findById(userId);

        if (!user.mfaEnabled) {
            return false;
        }

        const secret = await this.decryptSecret(user.mfaSecret);

        // Check if it's a backup code
        if (this.isBackupCode(token)) {
            return this.verifyBackupCode(userId, token);
        }

        // Verify TOTP
        return authenticator.verify({ token, secret });
    }

    // Recovery flow
    async initiateRecovery(
        userId: string,
        recoveryMethod: 'email' | 'phone'
    ): Promise<void> {
        const code = randomBytes(6).toString().slice(0, 6);

        await this.redis.setex(
            `recovery:${userId}`,
            600, // 10 minutes
            JSON.stringify({
                code,
                attempts: 0,
                method: recoveryMethod
            })
        );

        // Send code via selected method
        await this.sendRecoveryCode(userId, recoveryMethod, code);
    }
}
```

### 7. Credential Stuffing Protection

Protection against credential stuffing attacks.

```typescript
class CredentialStuffingProtection {
    constructor(
        private redis: RedisClient,
        private config: SecurityConfig
    ) {}

    async checkLoginAttempt(
        identifier: string,
        ip: string
    ): Promise<{ blocked: boolean; reason?: string }> {
        const identifierKey = `login:failed:${identifier}`;
        const ipKey = `login:failed:ip:${ip}`;
        const globalKey = 'login:failed:global';

        // Check IP rate limit
        const ipAttempts = await this.redis.get(ipKey);
        if (ipAttempts && parseInt(ipAttempts) >= this.config.maxIpAttempts) {
            return { blocked: true, reason: 'Too many attempts from this IP' };
        }

        // Check account rate limit
        const accountAttempts = await this.redis.get(identifierKey);
        if (accountAttempts && parseInt(accountAttempts) >= this.config.maxAccountAttempts) {
            return { blocked: true, reason: 'Account temporarily locked' };
        }

        // Check global rate limit
        const globalAttempts = await this.redis.get(globalKey);
        if (globalAttempts && parseInt(globalAttempts) >= this.config.maxGlobalAttempts) {
            return { blocked: true, reason: 'Service temporarily unavailable' };
        }

        return { blocked: false };
    }

    async recordFailedAttempt(
        identifier: string,
        ip: string
    ): Promise<void> {
        const now = Date.now();
        const windowStart = now - this.config.attemptWindow;

        // Increment counters with expiry
        await Promise.all([
            this.redis.incr(`login:failed:${identifier}`),
            this.redis.expire(`login:failed:${identifier}`, this.config.lockoutDuration),
            this.redis.incr(`login:failed:ip:${ip}`),
            this.redis.expire(`login:failed:ip:${ip}`, this.config.lockoutDuration)
        ]);

        // Check if this is a suspicious pattern
        if (await this.isSuspiciousPattern(identifier)) {
            await this.logSecurityEvent('CREDENTIAL_STUFFING_SUSPECTED', {
                identifier,
                ip
            });
        }
    }

    async recordSuccessfulLogin(userId: string, ip: string): Promise<void> {
        // Clear failed attempts
        await Promise.all([
            this.redis.del(`login:failed:${userId}`),
            this.redis.del(`login:failed:${ip}`),
            this.redis.del(`login:failed:email:${ip}`)
        ]);

        // Update last login
        await this.redis.setex(
            `lastlogin:${userId}`,
            30 * 24 * 60 * 60, // 30 days
            JSON.stringify({ ip, timestamp: Date.now() })
        );
    }

    private async isSuspiciousPattern(identifier: string): Promise<boolean> {
        // Check for high number of different accounts from same IP
        const accountCount = await this.redis.scard(`login:accounts:${identifier}`);
        return accountCount > 5;
    }
}
```

### 8. Magic Link Authentication

Passwordless authentication via email links.

```typescript
class MagicLinkService {
    constructor(
        private redis: RedisClient,
        private emailService: EmailService,
        private tokenService: TokenService
    ) {}

    async sendMagicLink(email: string): Promise<void> {
        // Rate limit
        const rateLimitKey = `magiclink:rate:${email}`;
        const attempts = await this.redis.incr(rateLimitKey);
        if (attempts > 5) {
            throw new RateLimitError('Too many requests');
        }
        await this.redis.expire(rateLimitKey, 3600);

        // Generate token
        const token = randomBytes(32).toString('hex');
        const hashedToken = createHash('sha256').update(token).digest('hex');

        // Store token
        await this.redis.setex(
            `magiclink:${hashedToken}`,
            900, // 15 minutes
            JSON.stringify({ email, createdAt: Date.now() })
        );

        // Send email
        const loginUrl = `${this.config.appUrl}/auth/magic-link/verify?token=${token}`;

        await this.emailService.send({
            to: email,
            template: 'magic-link',
            data: {
                loginUrl,
                expiresIn: '15 minutes'
            }
        });
    }

    async verifyMagicLink(token: string): Promise<TokenPair> {
        const hashedToken = createHash('sha256').update(token).digest('hex');
        const data = await this.redis.get(`magiclink:${hashedToken}`);

        if (!data) {
            throw new InvalidTokenError('Invalid or expired magic link');
        }

        const { email } = JSON.parse(data);

        // Delete used token
        await this.redis.del(`magiclink:${hashedToken}`);

        // Find user
        const user = await this.userService.findByEmail(email);
        if (!user) {
            throw new AuthError('User not found');
        }

        // Generate tokens
        return this.tokenService.generateTokens(user);
    }
}
```

### 9. Biometric Authentication

Biometric authentication với secure storage.

```typescript
class BiometricService {
    constructor(
        private keyStore: KeyStore,
        private userService: UserService
    ) {}

    // Register biometric credential
    async registerCredential(
        userId: string,
        credential: PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions
    ): Promise<{
        credentialId: string;
        publicKey: string;
    }> {
        // Generate key pair
        const keyPair = await crypto.subtle.generateKey(
            {
                name: 'ECDSA',
                namedCurve: 'P-256'
            },
            true,
            ['sign', 'verify']
        );

        // Export public key
        const publicKeyBuffer = await crypto.subtle.exportKey(
            'spki',
            keyPair.publicKey
        );
        const publicKey = Buffer.from(publicKeyBuffer).toString('base64');

        // Store key reference (not the private key)
        await this.keyStore.store(userId, {
            credentialId: credential.id,
            publicKey,
            counter: 0
        });

        return {
            credentialId: credential.id,
            publicKey
        };
    }

    // Authenticate with biometric
    async authenticate(
        userId: string,
        assertion: AuthenticatorAssertionResponse
    ): Promise<boolean> {
        const storedKey = await this.keyStore.get(userId);

        if (!storedKey) {
            throw new AuthError('No biometric credential registered');
        }

        // Verify signature
        const data = new TextEncoder().encode(
            JSON.stringify(assertion.authenticatorData) +
            assertion.clientDataJSON
        );

        const signatureValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
            { name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256' },
            storedKey.publicKey,
            assertion.signature,
            data
        );

        if (!signatureValid) {
            throw new AuthError('Biometric verification failed');
        }

        // Update counter
        await this.keyStore.update(userId, {
            counter: assertion.authenticatorData.counter
        });

        return true;
    }
}
```

### 10. Secure Token Storage

Secure storage considerations.

```typescript
// Token storage strategies
class TokenStorage {
    // Option 1: HttpOnly Cookies
    setTokenCookie(res: Response, token: string): void {
        res.cookie('access_token', token, {
            httpOnly: true,
            secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',
            sameSite: 'strict',
            maxAge: 15 * 60 * 1000 // 15 minutes
        });
    }

    // Option 2: Memory storage (for SPAs)
    // Tokens stored in memory, not localStorage
    // More secure against XSS

    // Option 3: Encrypted localStorage
    async setEncryptedToken(key: string, token: string): Promise<void> {
        const encrypted = await this.encrypt(token);
        localStorage.setItem(key, encrypted);
    }

    async getDecryptedToken(key: string): Promise<string | null> {
        const encrypted = localStorage.getItem(key);
        if (!encrypted) return null;
        return this.decrypt(encrypted);
    }
}

// Security considerations
const securityBestPractices = {
    accessTokenStorage: 'Memory (variable) - not localStorage',
    refreshTokenStorage: 'HttpOnly cookie or encrypted storage',
    avoidLocalStorage: 'LocalStorage is vulnerable to XSS',
    useCookies: 'Prefer HttpOnly cookies for web apps',
    encryptSensitive: 'Encrypt data before storing',
    clearOnLogout: 'Clear all tokens on logout',
    secureTransmission: 'Always use HTTPS'
};
